  "verbalization": "Enasidenib is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation, a condition that is also linked to Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(6;9)(p23;q34). This relationship is supported by the shared indication between Enasidenib and Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation, which in turn is connected to other leukemias through different therapeutic pathways. The evidence suggests that Enasidenib may exert its effects on a broader spectrum of leukemias, potentially through mechanisms that are not yet fully understood. The presence of multiple indirect pathways connecting Enasidenib to the target leukemia highlights the possibility of a shared biological mechanism or a broader therapeutic profile. The integration of these pathways underscores the potential for Enasidenib to be repurposed for treating this specific subtype of leukemia, though further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanism of action.",
